From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt DeVillier <matt.devillier@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 13:24:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] MdeModulePkg/SdMmcPciHcDxe: Don't force EmbeddedSlot for
 Bayhub

[ouroBIOS: commit c205cebb1a53 of MrChromebox's edk2, as it is]

Forcing EmbeddedSlot for every supported Bayhub/O2 Micro device ID
breaks removable SD card readers using the same parts: the initial
card detect is skipped, so empty slots are probed and fail, and the
hot-plug poll ignores the slot, so cards inserted later are never
detected.

Honor the slot type reported in the capability register, as before.
Soldered-down eMMC on a slot reporting removable is still probed as
long as card detect reports media present.

Signed-off-by: Matt DeVillier <matt.devillier@gmail.com>
---
 MdeModulePkg/Bus/Pci/SdMmcPciHcDxe/SdMmcPciHcDxe.c | 9 ---------
 1 file changed, 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Pci/SdMmcPciHcDxe/SdMmcPciHcDxe.c b/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Pci/SdMmcPciHcDxe/SdMmcPciHcDxe.c
index 17d04a4a009915a60735fd80519e19abf329288d..d3a178c2eddf55dfa5475be6c51ea64b14191a31 100644
--- a/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Pci/SdMmcPciHcDxe/SdMmcPciHcDxe.c
+++ b/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Pci/SdMmcPciHcDxe/SdMmcPciHcDxe.c
@@ -731,15 +731,6 @@ SdMmcPciHcDriverBindingStart (
       continue;
     }
 
-    //
-    // Bayhub/O2 Micro eMMC controllers may report a removable slot type in the
-    // SDHCI capability register even when the attached device is soldered-down
-    // eMMC. Treat Bayhub as EmbeddedSlot so we don't skip eMMC probing.
-    //
-    if (BhtHostPciSupport (PciIo)) {
-      Private->Capability[Slot].SlotType = EmbeddedSlot;
-    }
-
     Private->Slot[Slot].SlotType = Private->Capability[Slot].SlotType;
     if ((Private->Slot[Slot].SlotType != RemovableSlot) && (Private->Slot[Slot].SlotType != EmbeddedSlot)) {
       DEBUG ((DEBUG_INFO, "SdMmcPciHcDxe doesn't support the slot type [%d]!!!\n", Private->Slot[Slot].SlotType));
